## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` to dependencies using bun
- Updated `apps/web/package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `bun.lock` with dependency resolution

#### 2. Configured Analytics Component
- Modified `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate the Analytics component
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag (after the app content)
- Organized imports to comply with the project's linting rules (biome)

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- The Analytics component was imported from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- The component was placed at the end of the body to ensure it doesn't block page rendering
- No additional configuration is required - the component will automatically work when deployed to Vercel

### Framework Details
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.3.1 with App Router
- **Package Manager**: Bun (v1.3.14)
- **Analytics Package**: @vercel/analytics v2.0.1

### Files Modified
- `apps/web/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component
- `bun.lock` - Updated lock file with new dependency

### Verification
- Lint check passed for the modified layout.tsx file
- Import order fixed to match project's biome linting rules
- Package successfully installed and added to dependencies

### Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)
2. Visit the deployed site to generate analytics data
3. Check the browser's Network tab for requests to verify Analytics is working
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

The implementation follows best practices:
- Analytics component is placed at the end of body to not block rendering
- Preserves existing code structure and patterns
- Uses the latest stable version of @vercel/analytics
